WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.045
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for smooth reading.

2
00:00:03.495 --> 00:00:10.687
Here is the goal. On day ten, your child reads a short sentence never seen before, smoothly, the way it would be said.

3
00:00:11.137 --> 00:00:16.849
That is the goal. It is not a promise. This video tells you what the plan is, and how to use it.

4
00:00:17.649 --> 00:00:23.033
First, hear the difference. Word by word sounds like this. The, cat, sat, on, a, mat.

5
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:26.184
Smooth sounds like this. The cat sat on a mat.

6
00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:30.623
This plan is for a child who can already sound out short words.

7
00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:33.653
But the reading is slow. One word at a time.

8
00:00:34.103 --> 00:00:37.944
Or every word is sounded out again, even a word read a moment ago.

9
00:00:38.394 --> 00:00:41.769
Or single words are fine, but a whole sentence is not.

10
00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:48.318
Almost every new reader starts this way. It is a stage. It is not a sign that something is wrong.

11
00:00:48.768 --> 00:00:55.276
Sounding out takes all of a new reader's attention. Reading turns smooth when short words need no effort.

12
00:00:56.076 --> 00:01:00.580
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

13
00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:06.563
Day one is a short check. It shows you where the reading sticks. Day ten shows you what changed.

14
00:01:07.013 --> 00:01:12.270
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

15
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.933
And there are three moves. Your child learns one at a time.

16
00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:20.311
Move one. Sound it out in your head. Then say the word once.

17
00:01:22.861 --> 00:01:23.896
The word is cat.

18
00:01:24.696 --> 00:01:29.011
Move two. Scoop two or three words together, in one breath. The big dog.

19
00:01:29.711 --> 00:01:36.828
Move three. Read it three times. Once to work it out. Once to make it smooth. Once to make it sound like talking.

20
00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:44.804
Now, what to expect. The words are easy on purpose. Smooth reading comes from easy words, read again and again.

21
00:01:45.254 --> 00:01:50.598
Words come first. Then scoops of two or three words. Then whole sentences, and a story.

22
00:01:51.048 --> 00:01:57.575
There is no timer in this plan, and nobody counts words. Pressure makes reading worse. Smooth, not fast.

23
00:01:58.025 --> 00:02:03.489
Some days will need a second try. On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

24
00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:10.776
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

25
00:02:11.226 --> 00:02:15.794
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

26
00:02:16.244 --> 00:02:19.392
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

27
00:02:19.842 --> 00:02:23.139
Then your child does the rest alone, and reads to you at the end.

28
00:02:23.589 --> 00:02:28.468
On three of the days there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

29
00:02:28.918 --> 00:02:33.555
The voice waits, then reads it smoothly, so your child hears how it should sound.

30
00:02:34.355 --> 00:02:37.742
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and a few crayons.

31
00:02:38.192 --> 00:02:43.404
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about three minutes.
